### Invoice Service — manual test requests
# Works in VS Code (REST Client extension) and Visual Studio: click "Send Request" above each block.
# Start the stack first: docker compose up -d --build
#
# Every endpoint except the ERP webhook needs a token from Keycloak: 401 without one, 403 with the wrong role. Send 0a and
# 0b first; the requests below use their access_token. A token is valid for 5 minutes, then send 0a/0b again.
#
# Create saves the invoice as Bekliyor and queues it in erp_outbox (202); the ERP is not called in that request.
# Watch the sends live: docker compose logs -f invoice-service

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5090
@tokenUrl = http://localhost:8080/realms/fatura/protocol/openid-connect/token
@invoiceNumber = FTR-000001

### 0a) Token of the operator test user: reads and interventions, recorded under the name "operator"
# The fatura-test client (user name and password) is not in the default setup; for local tests add it to the running
# Keycloak once: .\manual-tests\keycloak\test-client-ekle.ps1
# @name operatorLogin
POST {{tokenUrl}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=fatura-test&username=operator&password=operator123

### 0b) Token of the order system (client credentials, no user): only it creates invoices
# @name orderSystemLogin
POST {{tokenUrl}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=siparis-sistemi&client_secret=dev-only-siparis-sistemi-secret-do-not-use-in-production

### 1) Create an invoice (202, status Bekliyor)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{orderSystemLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "customerCode": "C-001",
  "amount": 1250.50,
  "currency": "TRY",
  "invoiceDate": "2026-09-30"
}

### 2) The invoice as stored by the service
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceNumber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 3) Queue a failed invoice again (202; 409 if it is not Başarısız)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceNumber}}/resend
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4) One page of invoices, newest first (status, search = part of the number, page, pageSize 1-100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices?status=Bekliyor&search=FTR-0001&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4c) Only the stuck invoices (the ones the summary counts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices?stuck=true
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4a) How many invoices are in each status, and how many are stuck
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4b) The invoice with its erp_outbox entry, its events, its findings and the interventions made on it
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceNumber}}/details
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 3a) Queue several failed invoices again (1-100 numbers; one result per invoice: queued, not_found, not_failed, error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/resend
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "invoiceNumbers": ["FTR-000001", "FTR-000002"]
}

### 5) The same invoice on the ERP side (the ERP simulator has no token check)
GET http://localhost:5080/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceNumber}}

### 6) Invalid body (400, nothing is saved or sent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{orderSystemLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "customerCode": "",
  "amount": -5,
  "currency": "lira",
  "invoiceDate": "2026-09-30"
}

### 7) Start a reconciliation run now (202 with the run; 409 while another run is going)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliation-runs
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 8) One page of runs, newest first (without findings; pageSize 1-50)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliation-runs?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 7a) Without a token: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliation-runs

### 9) One run with its findings (replace 1 with a run id from 7 or 8)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliation-runs/1
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
